course: dictionary
lesson: 15367
title: Words for direction
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Southwards means towards the south. The ending -wards shows movement in a direction, like «walk homewards» or «look upwards». So when you see southwards, think: which way is the south, and is something moving that way?
explain: «The geese flew southwards in autumn.» The geese were moving towards the south. If you put the word «north» in its place, the sentence would say they flew the other way, so the meaning changes. Always check which direction the word points.
explain: On a map, the south is usually at the bottom of the page. Going southwards on a map means moving down it. Compass points are north, south, east and west, and south is the opposite of north.
fact: Southwards means towards the south.
fact: The ending -wards in a word often shows movement in a direction, like «upwards» and «homewards».
fact: On most maps, north is at the top and south is at the bottom, so going southwards means moving down the map.
fact: In autumn, many birds fly southwards to warmer places in the northern half of the world.
fact: Southward is also used, as in «a southward journey», and it means the same thing.
exercise: «The geese flew southwards in autumn.» Which way did the geese fly? | Round in a circle | *Towards the south | Towards the north | Up into the clouds
exercise: «The boat sailed southwards, past the rocks.» Find and copy the one word that tells the direction. | boat | *southwards | sailed | rocks
exercise: On a map, if you travel southwards, which way are you heading? | Up towards the top of the page | Left towards the edge | Right towards the sea | *Down towards the bottom of the page
test: «We walked southwards along the river until we reached the bridge.» Where were they going? | Up into the hills | Back home to the north | Under the bridge | *Towards the south
test: Which phrase means moving to the south? | *to head southwards | to stop completely | to sleep softly | to head northwards
exam: In autumn, many birds fly southwards to | a cold, dark cave | the top of the map | *warmer places | the bottom of the sea
